meta {
  name: update-alert-settings
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{baseURL}}/workspace/alert-settings
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "alertEmail": "alerts@pharmacy.com",
    "emailAlertsEnabled": true,
    "lowStockThreshold": 10,
    "nearExpiryDays": 30
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Update Alert Settings

  Updates workspace-wide inventory alert thresholds and email delivery configuration.

  ## Authorization

  Requires an authenticated `owner` or `admin`. Pharmacists receive `403 Forbidden`.

  ## Request Body

  | Field | Type | Required | Rules / Description |
  |-------|------|----------|---------------------|
  | `emailAlertsEnabled` | boolean | Yes | Enables or disables alert-email delivery. |
  | `alertEmail` | email string | Conditional | Required when email delivery is enabled. |
  | `lowStockThreshold` | integer | Yes | Must be greater than or equal to `0`. |
  | `nearExpiryDays` | integer | Yes | Must be greater than `0`. |

  ## Success Response

  **`200 OK`**

  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "Alert settings updated successfully",
    "data": null
  }
  ```

  ## Persistence Behavior

  - When email delivery is enabled, `alertEmail` is stored and `emailAlertsEnabledAt` is set to the current time.
  - When disabled, both stored email-delivery fields are cleared.
  - Workspace cache is invalidated immediately.
  - Persisted inventory alerts are re-evaluated using the new low-stock and near-expiry thresholds.

  ## Delivery Impact

  These settings affect future alert evaluation and worker-driven email delivery. Changing thresholds may immediately raise new alerts or resolve existing alerts.

  ## Errors

  | Status | Description |
  |--------|-------------|
  | `401 Unauthorized` | Authentication is invalid or membership is suspended. |
  | `403 Forbidden` | The authenticated member is not an owner or admin. |
  | `422 Unprocessable Entity` | Email configuration or numeric thresholds are invalid. |
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Settings persistence or alert synchronization failed unexpectedly. |
}
